<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tangaxuan II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1530">1530</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Tzintzicha Tangaxuan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tangaxuan II (died 1530) was the last independent cazonci, or ruler, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purepecha-empire">Purépecha Empire</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a> he submitted peacefully to the Spanish under Cristóbal de Olid in 1522, but he was later arrested by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuno-de-guzman">Nuño de Guzmán</a>, tortured to reveal treasure and executed in 1530.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tangaxuan-ii.jpg" alt="Tangaxuan II" width="320" height="489" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juan O'Gorman · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tangaxuan_II_being_executed.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
